# 26. Stable event time

Business event timestamps and pipeline execution timestamps are different concepts.

`occurred_at` must come from a stable domain timestamp or explicit source input.

Do not generate `occurred_at` using Date.now or equivalent during export if event determinism is required.

Pipeline execution time belongs in run metadata.

Do not include pipeline execution time in deterministic business event identity.

# 27. Event identity

Create deterministic event IDs.

The same logical event must receive the same ID when produced again.

Use stable canonical business keys.

Use a deterministic cryptographic hash where appropriate.

Do not use a random UUID when it prevents replay detection.

Document the identity rule concisely.

Test it.

# 28. Schema evolution

